1. Go to Administration, Login page <br />2. Check the checkbox button of 'admin/user account lockout'<br />3. Build a LDAP connection and create a user 'v' on LDAP server , and import the users from LDAP to local db, as the '<span>Include the domains'</span> users ,like 'Domain\v';
4. From the client ,login with user 'Domain\v' to make sure the account is worked;<br />5. Logout the user 'Domain\v' , and then login again with wrong password for over 5 times within 1 minute;<br />6. Check whether the 'User is locked out ' shows up;<br />7. Login the web GUI with user admin on the LAN client;<br />8. Go to User Status page , check that user 'Domain\v' is in the list of 'Locked out User Account list Check';
9. Clear the imported domain users, then imported the users from LDAP as 'No-domains' user, then repeat the step 4-8.
